{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.io.PrintWriter;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 998244353L;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n        if (k == 0) {\n            out.println(fact(n));\n            sc.close();\n            out.close();\n            return;\n        }\n        if (k > n - 1) {\n            out.println(0);\n            sc.close();\n            out.close();\n            return;\n        }\n        int c = (int)(n - k);\n        long answer = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= c; i++) {\n            long term = mult(paritySign(c - i), ncr(c, i), pow(i, n));\n            answer = add(answer, term);\n        }\n        answer = mult(answer, 2, ncr(n, c));\n        out.println(answer);\n        sc.close();\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    static long[] factArr = new long[1];\n    static long[] invFactArr = new long[1];\n    static {\n        factArr[0] = 1;\n        invFactArr[0] = 1;\n    }\n\n    static long fact(int n) {\n        if (n >= factArr.length) {\n            int oldLen = factArr.length;\n            long[] newFact = new long[n + 1];\n            long[] newInv = new long[n + 1];\n            System.arraycopy(factArr, 0, newFact, 0, oldLen);\n            System.arraycopy(invFactArr, 0, newInv, 0, oldLen);\n            for (int i = oldLen; i <= n; i++) {\n                newFact[i] = newFact[i - 1] * i % MOD;\n            }\n            newInv[n] = pow(newFact[n], (int)(MOD - 2));\n            for (int i = n - 1; i >= oldLen; i--) {\n                newInv[i] = newInv[i + 1] * (i + 1) % MOD;\n            }\n            factArr = newFact;\n            invFactArr = newInv;\n        }\n        return factArr[n];\n    }\n\n    static long invFact(int n) {\n        fact(n); // ensure computed\n        return invFactArr[n];\n    }\n\n    static long ncr(int n, int r) {\n        if (r < 0 || r > n) return 0;\n        return mult(fact(n), invFact(r), invFact(n - r));\n    }\n\n    static long paritySign(long k) {\n        return (k & 1) == 0 ? 1 : MOD - 1;\n    }\n\n    static long add(long a, long b) {\n        long v = a + b;\n        return v >= MOD ? v - MOD : v;\n    }\n\n    static long mult(long... x) {\n        long r = 1;\n        for (long v : x) r = r * v % MOD;\n        return r;\n    }\n\n    static long pow(long x, int e) {\n        if (e < 0) {\n            x = inv(x);\n            e = -e;\n        }\n        long res = 1;\n        while (e > 0) {\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) res = res * x % MOD;\n            x = x * x % MOD;\n            e >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static long inv(long x) {\n        return pow(x, (int)(MOD - 2));\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    if k == 0:\n        print(fact(n))\n        return\n    if k > n - 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    c = n - k\n    # Precompute factorials and inverse factorials up to n\n    precompute_fact(n)\n    answer = 0\n    for i in range(1, c + 1):\n        term = mult(parity_sign(c - i), ncr(c, i), pow(i, n, MOD))\n        answer = add(answer, term)\n    answer = mult(answer, 2, ncr(n, c))\n    print(answer)\n\nfact_arr = [1]\ninv_fact_arr = [1]\n\ndef precompute_fact(n):\n    global fact_arr, inv_fact_arr\n    if n < len(fact_arr):\n        return\n    old_len = len(fact_arr)\n    new_fact = [0] * (n + 1)\n    new_inv = [0] * (n + 1)\n    # Copy old values\n    for i in range(old_len):\n        new_fact[i] = fact_arr[i]\n        new_inv[i] = inv_fact_arr[i]\n    # Compute factorials\n    for i in range(old_len, n + 1):\n        if i == 0:\n            new_fact[i] = 1\n        else:\n            new_fact[i] = new_fact[i - 1] * i % MOD\n    # Compute inverse factorial using Fermat\n    new_inv[n] = pow(new_fact[n], MOD - 2, MOD)\n    for i in range(n - 1, old_len - 1, -1):\n        new_inv[i] = new_inv[i + 1] * (i + 1) % MOD\n    fact_arr = new_fact\n    inv_fact_arr = new_inv\n\ndef fact(n):\n    precompute_fact(n)\n    return fact_arr[n]\n\ndef inv_fact(n):\n    precompute_fact(n)\n    return inv_fact_arr[n]\n\ndef ncr(n, r):\n    if r < 0 or r > n:\n        return 0\n    return mult(fact(n), inv_fact(r), inv_fact(n - r))\n\ndef parity_sign(k):\n    return 1 if (k & 1) == 0 else MOD - 1\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    v = a + b\n    return v - MOD if v >= MOD else v\n\ndef mult(*args):\n    r = 1\n    for v in args:\n        r = r * v % MOD\n    return r\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.3708974620385561e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.00022516099852509797, -0.0009531007381156087, -2.384185506798530